{"metadata":{"name":"Sunan Abu Dawud","section":{"2":{"eng-name":"Prayer (Kitab Al-Salat)","ara-name":"كتاب الصلاة"}},"section_detail":{"2":{"hadithnumber_first":391,"hadithnumber_last":1160,"arabicnumber_first":391,"arabicnumber_last":1160}}},"hadiths":[{"hadithnumber":448,"arabicnumber":448,"text":"Rapporté par Abdullah ibn Abbas رضي الله عنه : Je n’ai pas reçu l’ordre de construire de hautes mosquées. Ibn Abbas a dit : « Vous les embellirez sûrement comme l’ont fait les Juifs et les Chrétiens. »","grades":[{"name":"Al-Albani","grade":"Sahih"},{"name":"Muhammad Muhyi Al-Din Abdul Hamid","grade":"Sahih"},{"name":"Zubair Ali Zai","grade":"Daif"}],"reference":{"book":2,"hadith":58},"chapter":{"id":12,"ara-name":"باب فِي بِنَاءِ الْمَسَاجِدِ","eng-name":"On (The Reward) Of Building Masajid","isFirstHadith":true}}]}